  "step_3": "The decision reason focuses on the maximum outcome (and, if equal, the minimum outcome) to determine preference. In this case, B has a higher maximum outcome (2500 > 2400), which aligns with the reason’s rule. The individual explicitly compared the maximum outcomes and highlighted the higher potential gain in B as a key factor. While the individual also referenced statistical expected value (which involves probabilities), the core justification for choosing B hinges on the superior maximum outcome, which is the primary criterion of the decision reason. The individual did not mention minimum outcomes (which are equal), but the reason does not require consideration of minimums when maximums differ. Therefore, the individual’s reasoning aligns with the decision reason’s rule. The use of the reason is strongly supported by the emphasis on the higher maximum outcome as a decisive factor.",
  "final_assessment_score": 95
